-- Protection (Lightsmith), from the simc `protection` list and Method's 12.1 priority.
--
-- Each glow is one rung with the terms the addon cannot read dropped, so a lit icon means
-- "this rung's readable conditions hold" and never "press this now": priority ORDER is not
-- expressible. Several of these light at once.
--
-- Hammer of Light and everything gated on `buff.hammer_of_light_ready` is absent on purpose --
-- it comes from Light's Deliverance, which is a TEMPLAR talent and not in this tree.
--
-- Check it, or turn it into a share string:
--     uv run python -m wowkb.smartglo check  projects/smart-glo/rules/protection-lightsmith.sg
--     uv run python -m wowkb.smartglo encode projects/smart-glo/rules/protection-lightsmith.sg

spec paladin.protection

-- Icy Veins ranks the free cast TWICE -- "below 50% Health" nine rungs above the plain proc --
-- and the split is the whole advice, because Word of Glory scales with MISSING health. Three
-- tiers, and the top two are URGENT: at 50% a free heal is being sat on, and at 30% it is
-- worth three Holy Power you were saving for mitigation.
--
-- The unconditional "you have a proc" rung is gone: Icy Veins ranks it 14th of 15, below
-- everything, and a rung that is true for most of a pull is what makes an icon unreadable.
glow "Word of Glory free and hurt"
  on     word_of_glory
  when   aura(shining_light)
  bind   health% < 80

glow "Word of Glory free and badly hurt"
  on     word_of_glory
  when   aura(shining_light)
  bind   health% < 50
  urgent

glow "Word of Glory paid, and desperate"
  on     word_of_glory
  when   holy_power >= 3
  bind   health% < 30
  urgent

-- The Lightsmith button. Two charges rotating Holy Bulwark and Sacred Weapon; which one is
-- next is not readable, so this marks the cast and leaves the choice to the player.
-- Not `ready()`: a mark meaning "this button is available" says what the swipe already says.
-- At the cap the next charge is being thrown away, which is a decision worth marking. The
-- CDM's own visual-source flags answer it without any charge count being read.
-- `next_armament` needs no term of its own. A subject IS the currently bound spell, so a rung
-- on Holy Bulwark attaches only while Bulwark is next and one on Sacred Weapon only while the
-- Weapon is -- the override arrives on `overrideSpellID` and the flush re-resolves against it.
-- These are the APL's two armament rungs with the unreadable half already answered.
glow "Holy Bulwark next and capped"
  on     holy_bulwark
  when   at_max_charges(holy_bulwark)
  urgent

-- The APL guards this side with `buff.sacred_weapon.remains<6|!buff.sacred_weapon.up`, and
-- neither half survives the charge economy: the shared pool recharges one charge per 60s and
-- the cast alternates, so two charges separate one Sacred Weapon from the next -- 120s against
-- a 20s buff. The buff is down for a minimum of 100s before the Weapon can come round again,
-- so `!up` is a tautology and `remains<6` is unreachable. Cap is the real condition on both
-- sides, and this is the Bulwark rung's twin for the other bound state.
glow "Sacred Weapon next and capped"
  on     sacred_weapon
  when   at_max_charges(sacred_weapon)
  urgent

-- `avengers_shield,if=buff.vanguard.up` -- the proc is the rung that outranks everything
-- below it. Off cooldown without the proc is an ordinary filler the swipe already shows.
glow "Avenger's Shield on Glory of the Vanguard"
  on     avengers_shield
  when   aura(glory_of_the_vanguard_1267203)

-- `avenging_wrath,if=cooldown.divine_toll.remains<=10` -- Divine Toll being ready is the
-- readable form, and it is the stricter half, so this holds wings rather than leaking them.
-- The Wrath rungs are GONE rather than shipped dark. `ready()` reads UNKNOWN for a spell you
-- do not know and the row is never laid out, so on a Sentinel build they could only ever be
-- two rungs of noise. The APL is no guide here -- it names Sentinel nowhere and plays the
-- Wrath side of the node -- so these are written against Sentinel directly.
glow "Sentinel with Divine Toll up"
  on     sentinel
  when   ready(sentinel) and ready(divine_toll)

-- The "Divine Toll inside Sentinel" rung is further down, under Sentinel and Divine Toll.
-- `not ready(sentinel)` is not what carries it: the cooldown outlasts the buff by minutes, so
-- it would be bright while wrong.

-- The BUILDERS. `judgment,if=full_recharge_time<=gcd*2` is a "you are about to waste a charge"
-- rung; at-the-cap is its readable half, strictly later than the APL's, so it under-marks
-- rather than over-marks. Crusader's Judgment adds the second charge -- without it this reads
-- as plain off-cooldown, which is honest either way.
glow "Judgment at cap"
  on     judgment
  when   at_max_charges(judgment)
  urgent

-- Hammer of Wrath rides the JUDGMENT row while Sentinel is up, and it takes the row with it:
-- `Attach.lua:94` keys a subject on `overrideSpellID` when one is set, so both Judgment rungs
-- above go dark the moment the swap happens -- measured, 21 attached rows inside the window
-- against 23 outside, with both Judgment rungs reading "no laid-out row". Ruination over Hand
-- of Gul'dan and Infernal Bolt over Shadow Bolt are the same shape, and they are written the
-- same way: a rung of the OVERRIDE's own.
--
-- No gate but readiness, and it does not over-light: the row only exists while the override
-- is on it, which is exactly the window in which Hammer of Wrath is castable.
--
-- `hammer_of_wrath` names the OVERRIDE here, 1241413, not the baseline 24275: where a spec
-- carries both, the symbol table prefers the id the Cooldown Manager lays out, which is the
-- only one a rung can bind to anyway.
--
-- ⚠ Protection knows Hammer of Wrath by no id at all -- it is in no spell book, it arrives
-- only as this override while Sentinel is up. What makes `ready` answerable is the bound row
-- itself, so a gate on the base spell would be refused where this one is not.
glow "Hammer of Wrath inside Sentinel"
  on     hammer_of_wrath
  when   ready(hammer_of_wrath)
  urgent

-- The filler builder is a CHOICE NODE, so both rungs ship and only the talented one can attach;
-- the other has no laid-out row and stays dark. Three charges is where a Protection rotation
-- actually leaks Holy Power, which is what makes the cap worth marking.
glow "Blessed Hammer at cap"
  on     blessed_hammer
  when   at_max_charges(blessed_hammer)
  urgent

glow "Hammer of the Righteous at cap"
  on     hammer_of_the_righteous
  when   at_max_charges(hammer_of_the_righteous)
  urgent

-- Sealed, not gated. `aura()` reads the CDM's alert edges, so it needs a laid-out row raising
-- them and answers UNKNOWN -- dark -- when the Tracked Buffs checkbox for this one is off. A
-- presence bind hands the question to an AuraContainer instead, which reads the unit directly
-- and needs no row at all. The bind slot is free on both rungs, so it costs nothing.
glow "Blessed Hammer on Blessed Assurance"
  on     blessed_hammer
  bind   blessed_assurance.up

glow "Hammer of the Righteous on Blessed Assurance"
  on     hammer_of_the_righteous
  bind   blessed_assurance.up

-- Not the APL's `buff.divine_guidance.stack>=5` rung but the practical one: Consecration is
-- worth pressing when you are not standing in it and it is off cooldown.
--
-- `consecration` names two tracked rows, so the aura side takes the suffixed form and says
-- which. The subject resolves on its own now: the ability namespace lets the CDM's own row win
-- a name inside its spec, so `consecration` is 26573, the cast, and no longer 81297.
glow "Consecration when you are not in it"
  on     consecration
  when   ready(consecration) and not aura(consecration_188370)

-- Two rungs on the same button, and the second is the first with its requirement lowered.
-- At the cap you press regardless, because the next generator overcaps. With the mitigation
-- buff DOWN it is worth pressing at the castable minimum instead, so the missing buff is what
-- buys the drop from 5 to 3. Both light the same mark, and at 5 with the buff down both hold.
--
-- `>= 5` rather than `== 5` so a talent that raises the cap cannot silently step over it.
glow "Shield of the Righteous at cap"
  on     shield_of_the_righteous
  when   holy_power >= 5
  urgent

-- `on` and `aura()` read DIFFERENT namespaces, so the same word means the button in one and
-- the mitigation buff in the other. The cooldown row carries the buff as a linked spell, which
-- is what makes them one subject.
glow "Shield of the Righteous with the buff down"
  on     shield_of_the_righteous
  when   holy_power >= 3 and not aura(shield_of_the_righteous)

-- "Consecration if everything else is on cooldown to refresh the duration" -- the third
-- Consecration case, and the only one that fires while you are still standing in it with no
-- Divine Guidance banked. The readable half is the builders being down; Blessed Hammer and
-- Hammer of the Righteous are a choice node, so the untalented one reads UNKNOWN and cannot
-- make this true on its own.
glow "Consecration to refresh, nothing else up"
  on     consecration
  when   ready(consecration) and not ready(judgment) and not ready(avengers_shield)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- baseline builders
--
-- The KB's own loop is "never Holy-Power-cap, keep Consecration under you, keep Shield of the
-- Righteous rolling", and all three of these are rotational BUILDERS rather than situational
-- buttons. The swipe already says a builder is available; what it cannot say is that you also
-- have room for what it generates, which is the whole of the advice here.

glow "Judgment with room to spend"
  on     judgment
  when   ready(judgment) and holy_power < 5

glow "Blessed Hammer with room to spend"
  on     blessed_hammer
  when   ready(blessed_hammer) and holy_power < 5

glow "Hammer of the Righteous with room to spend"
  on     hammer_of_the_righteous
  when   ready(hammer_of_the_righteous) and holy_power < 5

-- Tighter, because Glory of the Vanguard makes this hand back up to three at once.
glow "Avenger's Shield with room to spend"
  on     avengers_shield
  when   ready(avengers_shield) and holy_power <= 2

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- Sentinel and Divine Toll
--
-- Divine Toll is ~1 min and Sentinel ~2 min, which Righteous Protector halves -- so with that
-- talent they pair 1:1 and without it Sentinel lands on every other Toll.

-- Sitting on Sentinel because the Toll was misfired is a real loss, and the APL uses the same
-- shape for the Wrath case: a cooldown far enough out that waiting costs more than desyncing.
glow "Sentinel anyway, Divine Toll is far off"
  on     sentinel
  when   ready(sentinel) and not ready(divine_toll)
  bind   divine_toll.cooldown > 30s

-- `active()` rather than `aura()` or a bind. Sentinel HAS a laid-out row, so `active()` can
-- ask it directly whether it is currently showing an aura rather than a cooldown -- which is
-- the question, and it needs no aura id at all.
--
-- ⚠ The aura id is exactly what this rung cannot have. `Symbols.auraNames` carries one
-- `sentinel`, 1253599, and that is the HUNTER Marksmanship hero talent; the Paladin row in
-- the ability inventory has no aura id at all. A `sentinel.up` bind therefore resolved
-- through the ability-table fallback and armed a container on 389539, the SPELL id, which no
-- aura ever matches -- and a sealed bind that finds nothing fails dark, so it read exactly
-- like a condition that was false.
glow "Divine Toll inside Sentinel"
  on     divine_toll
  when   ready(divine_toll) and active(sentinel)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- Consecration payload
--
-- Divine Guidance banks a payload on the NEXT Consecration -- "for each Holy Power ability
-- cast, your next Consecration deals damage or healing immediately". At the cap that is a
-- reason to recast while it is still down, which the not-standing-in-it rung cannot say.
glow "Consecration at five Divine Guidance"
  on     consecration
  bind   divine_guidance.stacks >= 5

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the panic buttons
--
-- A TRAINING aid, and it teaches the wrong reflex if left on: a defensive is better pressed
-- ahead of damage than after it, and these fire after. They exist to make the buttons
-- familiar, not to time them.
--
-- Every one is suppressed while another major is already up, so the set never asks you to
-- stack two. Sentinel is in that guard through `active()` rather than `aura()`: nothing tracks
-- it as a buff, but its own cooldown row records that its dial is drawing an aura, and that
-- verdict is a plain boolean. The bind slot could not have carried it -- it is spent on the
-- health threshold, and a glow holds one sealed leaf.
-- Holy Bulwark is in, under the suffix that says which row: 432607 carries the absorb and
-- 432496 the stat package, so the shield is the one worth guarding on.

glow "Ardent Defender when hurt"
  on     ardent_defender
  when   ready(ardent_defender) and not aura(ardent_defender) and not aura(guardian_of_ancient_kings) and not aura(divine_shield) and not active(sentinel) and not aura(holy_bulwark_432607)
  bind   health% < 70

glow "Guardian of Ancient Kings when hurt"
  on     guardian_of_ancient_kings
  when   ready(guardian_of_ancient_kings) and not aura(ardent_defender) and not aura(guardian_of_ancient_kings) and not aura(divine_shield) and not active(sentinel) and not aura(holy_bulwark_432607)
  bind   health% < 70

-- ⚠ Divine Shield is only a TANK defensive with Final Stand. Without it the immunity drops
-- threat and the pull walks past you into the group, so an unconditional panic rung here is a
-- wipe button with a friendly face. `talent()` reads the trait config, so the rung simply
-- cannot fire on a build that has not taken it.
--
-- Blessing of Protection is absent for the same reason and has no equivalent rescue: it drops
-- threat too, and nothing makes it not. Blessing of Spellwarding is the one immunity a tank
-- may press freely -- the KB calls it "no threat concern" -- which is why it is here and its
-- choice-node partner is not.
glow "Divine Shield when hurt"
  on     divine_shield
  when   talent(final_stand) and ready(divine_shield) and not aura(ardent_defender) and not aura(guardian_of_ancient_kings) and not aura(divine_shield) and not active(sentinel) and not aura(holy_bulwark_432607)
  bind   health% < 70

glow "Blessing of Spellwarding when hurt"
  on     blessing_of_spellwarding
  when   ready(blessing_of_spellwarding) and not aura(ardent_defender) and not aura(guardian_of_ancient_kings) and not aura(divine_shield) and not active(sentinel) and not aura(holy_bulwark_432607)
  bind   health% < 70

-- Lower, because a ten-minute button lit at 70% teaches you to burn it on a scratch.
-- This row is laid out as Lay on Hands overridden by 471195, which the ability tables do not
-- name. The name still works: the client calls both ids "Lay on Hands", so the row answers to
-- the base as well as the override and a rung written on 633 binds either way.
glow "Lay on Hands when nearly dead"
  on     lay_on_hands
  when   ready(lay_on_hands) and not aura(ardent_defender) and not aura(guardian_of_ancient_kings) and not aura(divine_shield) and not active(sentinel) and not aura(holy_bulwark_432607)
  bind   health% < 50

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------ confirm while logged in
--
-- Nothing here needs a command run at the right moment. The attach flush writes the whole row
-- inventory to the capture whenever the row set changes, and a Sentinel window changes it
-- twice, so play a pull with `/sg procs dim` set and read it back afterwards.
--
--   * Which id the Cooldown Manager writes as the Judgment row's override. If it is 24275
--     rather than 1241413, this rung's subject is wrong and the swap is one line.
--   * Both Judgment rungs detaching on the way in and re-attaching on the way out, which is
--     what makes this rung necessary rather than a duplicate.
--   * The proc-alert state on a row that procced -- the client's own alpha, so a dimming that
--     did nothing and a proc that never fired stop looking alike.
